This directory is bind-mounted read-only into the `nginx` service at /etc/nginx/ssl (see
docker/docker-compose.yml). It intentionally ships empty: docker/config/nginx.conf does not
reference any certificate files by default, so nginx serves plain HTTP on port 80 out of the
box and this directory can stay empty for local/dev use.

To enable TLS termination in nginx for production use:

  1. Place your certificate and private key here, e.g.:
       docker/config/ssl/fullchain.pem
       docker/config/ssl/privkey.pem
     (Do not commit real certificates/keys to version control.)

  2. Add a `listen 443 ssl;` server block to docker/config/nginx.conf referencing them:
       ssl_certificate     /etc/nginx/ssl/fullchain.pem;
       ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/privkey.pem;

  3. Restart the `nginx` service: `docker compose restart nginx`.
